schema: '0.4'
id: abcjs-01-lead-sheet-simple-score
type: interactive
quality: high
solution: abcjs
category: music-notation
variant: lead-sheet-simple-score
references:
- references/fim/overview/music-audio-ml/abcjs.md
- references/fim/solution/abcjs.md
prompt:
  system: |-
    You generate abcjs browser music-notation artifacts. Output only a complete self-contained HTML document with inline CSS and JavaScript. Do not use markdown fences or explanations.
  text: |
    Create the lead sheet and simple score for abcjs.

    Scenario:
    Create a concise lead sheet or simple score that a musician can sight-read immediately. Use 8 to 16 bars, a clear title, tempo, chord symbols, one primary melody, a simple accompaniment or tab line when the solution supports it, and a final cadence.

    Implementation requirements:
    - Use this solution source: ABC v2.1 notation text embedded in the page.
    - Render with abcjs.renderAbc using abcjs v6 from a CDN, and use abcjs audio or synth controls when playback is requested.
    - Syntax contract: Use valid ABC headers and body syntax: X, T, C, M, L, Q, K, optional V voices, chord symbols in quotes, repeats, endings, lyrics with w:, and barlines.
    - Musical coherence contract: pitches, chords, lyrics, articulations, and form must describe one coherent musical example, not disconnected fragments.
    - Measure-duration contract: every measure, part, voice, layer, sequence, or track must sum to the declared time signature; pickups, tuplets, ties, repeats, and final bars must be explicitly represented.
    - Clef/key contract: declare initial clefs, keys, time signatures, part names, and any changes in the solution-native structure; transposed parts must use correct written key signatures and accidentals.
    - Playback/render compatibility contract: include the exact load, render, playback, export, or fallback path expected for this solution and explain unsupported playback honestly inside code comments or metadata.
    - Accessibility contract: include title, instrument labels, measure numbers or landmarks, keyboard-operable controls when interactive, and text alternatives for screen readers.
    - Provide renderTune(), updateTune(abc), transposeTune(semitones), startPlayback(), stopPlayback(), exportAbc(), and teardown() hooks with clear error output for parse warnings.
    - Keep the ABC source visible in a read-only panel so the notation remains inspectable and screen-reader friendly.
    - Keep the musical idea simple but complete: phrase structure, chords, melody, and ending must agree.
    - Use one stable key and meter unless a brief pickup or final bar requires explicit handling.
    - Include lyrics, rehearsal text, or chord names when the solution can encode them.
    - Include deterministic sample score data directly in the artifact; do not depend on private credentials or remote score files except public library CDNs or clearly marked placeholders.
    - Output only the final artifact requested by the system message, with no commentary outside the artifact.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
output:
  text_format: html
  artifact_kind: abcjs-html-score
  formats:
  - format: html
  - format: svg
  - format: midi
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - 'Format validity: prompt YAML parses as schema 0.4 and the generated artifact is exactly the requested output with no markdown fences.'
  - 'Syntax: generated artifact uses valid abcjs syntax or API calls and includes required parser, compiler, renderer, service, or font setup.'
  - 'Musical coherence: melody, harmony, rhythm, lyrics, annotations, and form describe one coherent score suitable for the scenario.'
  - 'Measure duration: every measure in every part, voice, layer, sequence, or track sums to the declared meter; pickups, tuplets, ties, repeats, and final bars are handled explicitly.'
  - 'Clefs and keys: initial clefs, keys, time signatures, part names, transpositions, and any changes are declared in solution-native fields.'
  - 'Playback/render compatibility: load, render, compile, export, playback, cursor, soundfont, service auth, font, CORS, or fallback behavior is correct for the solution.'
  - 'Accessibility: artifact includes title, part labels, text fallback or source view, keyboard-operable controls when interactive, and screen-reader friendly summaries.'
  - 'Robustness: artifact handles missing fonts/assets, malformed notation, large or dense scores, responsive layout, and cleanup or teardown without runtime failure.'
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria: The prompt YAML and generated artifact use the required schema, file format, solution syntax, parser or API contract, and contain no markdown fences or malformed structures.
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria: The score covers the requested scenario with complete musical content, annotations, metadata, parts, playback or export path, and solution-specific capabilities.
  - name: Visual/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria: The notation structure, engraving or layout hierarchy, labels, spacing, page or responsive behavior, and instructional affordances are clear and professional.
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria: The artifact handles dense material, edge notation, transposition, accessibility, missing assets, service/auth errors, render fallback, playback constraints, and teardown safely.
  pass_conditions:
  - YAML parses successfully and all prompt file bytes are ASCII-only.
  - Rubric weights are exactly 30, 30, 25, and 15, summing to 100.
  - Generated artifact passes solution syntax validation or the closest practical parser/compiler/load check.
  - Every measure duration is consistent with declared meter across all parts, voices, tracks, layers, or sequences.
  - Clefs, keys, time signatures, part names, transpositions, and accidentals are explicit and musically coherent.
  - Playback, render, compile, export, font, service, or fallback compatibility checks are satisfied for the target solution.
  - Accessibility and robustness checklist items are satisfied; no rubric dimension scores zero.
tags:
- fim
- music-notation
- abcjs
- lead-sheet-simple-score
- interactive
- lead-sheet
- simple-score
